  - experiment-orchestration
abstract: >-
  The conductor takes a dispatched procedure from a system of record and walks
  it across a beamline, one step at a time. It claims the hardware a step
  names before writing to it, refuses a step whose records another walk is
  already holding, and reports how each step ended. Everything above the
  adapters composes a procedure through seams shaped like the verbs it uses,
  so which control protocol a deployment runs is a choice made at its
  entrypoint rather than a fact the domain knows. It is a client of the
  keeper, a separate deployable bound to it by prose and two metadata keys
  rather than by a shared package.
